+# Health-check type extraction
+
+Moved `Checker`, `CheckerFunc`, and the unchanged `CheckerFunc.Check` method to
+`server/util/healthcheck/checker`, a leaf Go library importing only `context`.
+`server/interfaces` retains type aliases, preserving Go type identity and existing
+call sites. Healthcheck now imports the leaf directly. Updated both existing BUILD
+files and added the leaf BUILD file by hand.
+
+## Premise and measurements
+
+Before editing, source inspection confirmed healthcheck used interfaces only for
+these two types. Querying the closure of its other nine library dependencies showed
+that interfaces uniquely contributed 246 first-party labels and 1,299 external
+labels. The reduction is substantial, so the extraction proceeded.
+
+Identical queries were used before and after:
+
+```sh
+bazel query 'deps(//server/util/healthcheck)' | wc -l
+bazel query 'kind("rule", deps(//server/util/healthcheck))'
+```
+
+The query output was saved and counted by `//` (first-party) and `@` (external)
+prefix; external labels include source files, not just rules.
+
+| Metric | Before | After | Change |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| All dependency labels (`deps` / `wc -l`) | 4,602 | 3,061 | -1,541 |
+| First-party dependency labels | 302 | 60 | -242 |
+| External dependency labels | 4,300 | 3,001 | -1,299 |
+| All dependency rules | 1,403 | 1,044 | -359 |
+| First-party dependency rules | 198 | 49 | -149 |
+| External dependency rules | 1,205 | 995 | -210 |
+| Go + BUILD LOC in interfaces, healthcheck, and new leaf | 2,587 | 2,603 | +16 |
+
+The survey's ~152 first-party rule reduction was close; its ~70 external label
+estimate understated the actual reduction. No binary size claim is made.
+
+## Validation
+
+`gofmt` and `git diff --check` passed. The 31-target build passed (exit 0,
+5,761.562 seconds / about 96 minutes). The healthcheck test passed (exit 0,
+17.762 seconds; both shutdown/signal test cases in the single Bazel test target).
+
+The requested full-repository query
+`bazel query 'rdeps(//..., //server/util/healthcheck, 1)'` failed during repository
+fetch: `default_execution_image`'s `docker build --no-cache` exceeded its timeout.
+The query was interrupted after that error when it started another unrelated
+Docker image fetch. A package-wildcard fallback was also narrowed to avoid image
+targets. No repository/dependency configuration was modified to bypass the error.
+
+Consumer packages were selected with
+`rg -l -F '"//server/util/healthcheck"' --glob BUILD --glob BUILD.bazel .`, then Bazel
+queried their rules with `attr("deps", "//server/util/healthcheck:healthcheck(,| |\\]|$)", set(<consumer package wildcards> //server/util/healthcheck:*))`.
+This succeeded and found 26 direct consumers, including the local healthcheck test.
+The equivalent interfaces query succeeded and found 283 direct consumers; the
+requested three binary proxies were used for interfaces validation.
+
+A depth-one `rdeps` query restricted to the selected healthcheck consumers then
+passed (exit 0, 27 labels: healthcheck itself plus the same 26 consumers).
+`rdeps(set(//server/cmd/buildbuddy:buildbuddy_lib
+//enterprise/server/cmd/server:server_lib
+//enterprise/server/cmd/executor:executor_lib //server/interfaces),
+//server/interfaces, 1)` also passed. Bazel includes the universe's transitive
+closure, so this returned interfaces and its direct dependents reachable through
+those proxies (136 labels: interfaces plus 135 direct dependents).
+
+Background validation (local execution, two jobs):
+
+```sh
+bazel build --jobs=2 --keep_going --target_pattern_file=/tmp/healthcheck-build.targets
+bazel test --jobs=2 //server/util/healthcheck:healthcheck_test
+```
+
+The target-pattern file contains the 26 healthcheck consumers plus interfaces, the
+new leaf, and `//server/cmd/buildbuddy:buildbuddy`,
+`//enterprise/server/cmd/server:buildbuddy`, and
+`//enterprise/server/cmd/executor:executor` (31 unique targets). Logs are in
+`/tmp/healthcheck-build.log` and `/tmp/healthcheck-test.log`.
+
+## Dependencies and scope
+
+No shared dependency files were edited. Interfaces retains all its existing
+external dependencies; this changes only which closure healthcheck reaches.
+No external module became unused. Evidence: saved output from
+`bazel query 'deps(//server/interfaces)'` contains all 1,299 external labels in
+`before_healthcheck_deps - after_healthcheck_deps` (set comparison: 1,299 retained,
+0 missing). `git diff -- server/interfaces/BUILD` also confirms every old dependency
+entry remains; only the new leaf was added.
+
+Only the requested `result.md` is outside the listed implementation scope. No
+other call sites were migrated, and no runtime health/shutdown logic was changed.
+The existing shutdown and signal tests passed; no additional behavior tests
+are needed for moving the unchanged definitions and adding type aliases.
+
+Unused Docker build cache and the image generated by the failed repository query
+were reclaimed to free disk space during the build. No source configuration changed.
+
+## Built targets
+
+Contents of `/tmp/healthcheck-build.targets`:
+
+```text
